   "widgets_values": [
    "## Restyle a track (cover its melody) - YuE 2\n\n**A reference track in, the same tune out in a new style.** The one restyle route in the repo: SheetSage2\ntranscribes the reference's **melody** into ABC notation (`SheetSage2AudioToABC`, previewed on node 6) and\n`YuE2GenerateMusic(mode='melody')` re-renders from it with a **style and lyrics you write**. ACE-Step's\nstyle flow only *keeps* a reference (E5), so this is the capability it cannot reach - and the user's ears\nconfirm the cover is recognisably the reference's tune, restyled (E12d).\n\n- **the reference** goes on `LoadAudio` (any audio file in ComfyUI's `input/`); a 30 s reference covers in\n  **65 s**.\n- **`STYLE`** (node 7) is the idiom to change it into - the shipped example is industrial rock.\n- **`LYRICS`** (node 7) is new text: the reference's *melody* is kept, its *words* are not. New words only land when the source has a sung vocal line - an instrumental's transcribed `Vocal` line is all rests, and E22's added lyric was not sung.\n- **`max_duration` must be at least the reference's length.** The model chooses the duration itself and this\n  only bounds it - unlike ACE-Step, where the duration is a constant we set. So **you cannot target a length**: the cap only bounds, and the model stops when its ABC phrase ends (E22: a 30 s instrumental at cap 30 came out 27.7 s with a 188-word lyric, 29.5 s with none).\n- **`mode`** is `melody` (a cover); `full` writes a new song instead.\n- **node 6 (`PreviewAny`) shows the ABC** that SheetSage2 transcribed - the way to see whether the melody was\n  read at all. It is two-voice (`Vocal` + `Ins`); an all-rests `Vocal` line means the reference was\n  instrumental.\n\n**Licence: `cc-by-nc-4.0` (`Comfy-Org/YuE2`) - non-commercial, research only.** And **a transcript is not a presence test**:\nWhisper read 0-19 words on takes whose vocal the ears plainly hear (E12c), so never call a take instrumental\nfrom a transcript.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S22** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E12/E12d/E22** in `audio/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*\n"
   ],
   "properties": {},
   "order": 0
  }
